{
  "_doc": "Icon Kit layers. Every layer is a square picture on the SAME canvas with the SAME centre: plate (grey, tinted per class) -> glow + glyph (cut to the plate) -> state effects -> frame. Entries have `placeholder` (drawn SVG, kept as the fallback) and, after tools/import-layers.py, `file` (256 px WebP) + `small` (64 px). Frames: `style` painted (art), line (thin / hairline: painted gold art when imported; the drawn line version takes any colour, spec.frameColor) or none; `inner` = the measured opening (radius or half-width, share of the canvas) \u2014 plates grow to it and glyphs grow with it; `placeholderInner` = the drawn placeholder's opening; `class` = which class's themed frame it is (themes.json classes[].frame). Plates: `radius` = the painted plate's own radius, `placeholderRadius` the drawn one's; the kit scales the plate so it tucks just under whichever frame is on. Round 2 (2026-11-27): Codex's 'hairline' paintings came out as ornamental rings, so they are the 'filigree' frame; its thin-square was a medium frame and was dropped. Hairline (both) and thin-square use the drawn line until repainted.",
